\cf0 Step 1: \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 Hi everyone. I built a system that takes a video idea, plans and generates the shots, reviews the results, and turns everything into a finished video.\
\
For this demo, I\'92ll quickly show you the process and the final output.\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \uc0\u11835 \
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Step 2: \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 The process starts with a simple request.\
\
Instead of giving Conductor a long prompt every time, I moved the recurring instructions into the workflow.\
\
Now I can give it a short request, and the system handles the rest of the process.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\uc0\u11835 \
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Step 3: \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 The first thing the system does is look at this existing video library.\
\
This library gives the system examples of different video styles, pacing, transitions, and storytelling.\
\
It uses those references as inspiration to plan a new video, rather than copying one directly.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\uc0\u11835 \
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Step 4: \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 After reviewing the references, the system breaks the idea into individual shots.\
\
For this video, it created four shots with their own purpose, timing, copy, and visual direction.\
\
Here, I\'92m showing three of them: the initial brief, the campaign idea, and how that idea expands into different marketing assets.\
\
For this project, the system chose HyperFrames because the video needed precise text, UI, and layout instead of generative footage.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 For other videos, it can use models available through Fal when the shot needs things like cinematic movement or generated footage.\
\
The idea is to choose the method that best fits the shot, instead of using the same model for everything.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\uc0\u11835 \
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Step 5: \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Once the individual shots are ready, they\'92re combined into the final video.\
The workflow then checks things like timing, transitions, audio, and the final output before considering the video complete.\
\
\uc0\u11835 \
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 Step 6: \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 For every finished video, the system creates its own reverse-engineering document.\
This records how the video was made, including the prompts, structure, methods used, revisions, and key learnings.\
The workflow also checks that this file exists before the video can be marked complete.\
\
\uc0\u11835 \
\
\pard\pardeftab560\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

